   "text": {
    "L1": "Natural resources come from nature and are used by living things.",
    "L2": "Air is not nothing. It takes up space, and it has weight.",
    "L3": "Air is a resource even though it is free. It helps us breathe, dry things and use wind.",
    "L4": "Water, sunlight, soil and forests are natural resources too.",
    "L5": "Water is used for drinking and farming. Sunlight helps plants make food and gives warmth.",
    "L6": "Soil holds plants and gives them water and minerals. Forests give wood, fruits, leaves, honey and medicines.",
    "L7": "Here is a test for air. A dry tissue is fixed inside an empty glass and the glass is turned upside down.",
    "L8": "Push the glass straight into water, then lift it out. The tissue stays dry because air took up space and kept water out."
   },
